    "probe_text": "The YAML confirms the pipeline. Here is the complete ordered list for **`POST /api/owners`**.\n\n## Gate (before any step runs)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the whole endpoint requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` (`composition.authorize`). No role \u2192 rejected before the pipeline starts.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n**Normalization / validation phase (no transaction yet):**\n\n1. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 binds the request body (the *only* `@RequestBody` read). Strips separators and converts telephone to E.164 (assumes `+61`, drops a leading `0`; requires the right national digit count). Bad number \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"telephone\"])` \u2192 **400**. Republishes the normalized body.\n2. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 if email present, must match the email regex or **400** (`[\"email\"]`); then lower-cases it in place. Absent/blank email is skipped.\n3. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** \u2014 trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE) in place.\n4. **ValidateOwnerFields** \u2014 requires non-blank `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone`, then runs JSR-380 bean validation on the DTO (size/pattern constraints on each field). Any violations \u2192 **400** with body `{\"errors\":[...field names...]}`.\n5. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 if postcode present, must fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region \u2192 any 4 digits). Invalid \u2192 **400** (`[\"postcode\"]`). Absent postcode skipped.\n\n**Business-rule + persistence phase (all `govern: [ transaction ]`, one commit at end):**\n\n6. **EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity** \u2014 derives identity key (E.164 telephone + email + optional household id) and scans all owners; exact match \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n7. **EnsureCityHasCapacity** \u2014 if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n8. **ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 effective date = supplied `registrationDate` else server's today; rolls a weekend forward (Sat\u2192Mon, Sun\u2192Mon). Publishes the adjusted date. *(No rejection; a computation.)*\n9. **EnsureDailyOwnerCapacity** \u2014 if that resolved day already has \u2265 100 registrations \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n10. **BuildOwner** \u2014 MapStruct maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity (id and pets ignored).\n11. **AssignOwnerHousehold** \u2014 only if `sharesHousehold=true`: sets a household id on the new owner **and writes it back onto matching existing owners** (`save` on *other* rows \u2014 a side-effect on unrelated records).\n12. **AssignOwnerHouseholdSize** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing members sharing the household id + 1.\n13. **AssignOwnerNamesakeCount** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n14. **AssignOwnerMembershipLevel** \u2014 level = 1, +1 if email present, +1 if namesakeCount == 0, capped at 3.\n15. **AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > 80 owners already registered for the resolved day.\n16. **ApplyOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 stamps the resolved (weekend-adjusted) date onto the owner.\n17. **AssignOwnerCustomerCode** \u2014 assigns `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN = current per-city owner count + 1.\n18. **SaveOwner** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the primary persist (generates the id).\n19. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel) after save.\n20. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps the saved owner to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with a **`Location: /api/owners/{id}`** header. The transaction commits here.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- The rejection order is deliberate: **telephone \u2192 email \u2192 address normalization \u2192 required-field/bean validation \u2192 postcode \u2192 uniqueness (409) \u2192 city cap (409) \u2192 daily cap (429)**. So a bad body is a 400 before any capacity/duplicate check runs.\n- **Side-effects on other rows:** step 11 can modify existing owners' household ids even though this is a \"create.\"\n- Escalation handlers map: `InvalidOwnerFields`\u2192400, `DuplicateOwnerIdentity`/`CityAtCapacity`\u2192409, `DailyOwnerLimit`\u2192429, and (surprisingly) `DataIntegrityViolationException`\u2192**404**.\n- Bean validation runs against the **DTO** (`OwnerFieldsDto`), not the `Owner`/`Person` entity annotations, which only fire if Hibernate validates on persist.\n\nThis reflects the current code, not the shorter worked example in AGENTS.md \u2014 the real pipeline is 20 steps with substantial business logic."
